9f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068882 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f095dc29-06a2-59bf-8997-6e524951d317"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068883 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f7541a79-898f-52f6-9741-385d5ef8e2c1" "question-ff75b330-ecd4-5fa0-b36d-564d6c66e864"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-86933fa6-f8f7-5354-b325-40dd23c73f55" :question/id #uuid "86933fa6-f8f7-5354-b325-40dd23c73f55" :question/math-academy-id "q-75921" :question/problem "Solve for $x$ where $\\frac{x-2}{2x}+\\frac{x-4}{2x}=\\frac{5x-6}{2x}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that $x=0$ is an excluded solution since division by $0$ is undefined. \n\nWe multiply both sides of the equation by $2x,$ and simplify: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-2}{2x}+\\frac{x-4}{2x} & =\\frac{5x-6}{2x} \\\\ 2x\\cdot (\\frac{x-2}{2x}+\\frac{x-4}{2x}) & =n\\cdot (\\frac{5x-6}{2x}) \\\\ 2x\\cdot \\frac{x-2}{2x}+2x\\cdot \\frac{x-4}{2x} & =2x\\cdot \\frac{5x-6}{2x} \\\\ \\cancel{2x}\\cdot \\frac{x-2}{\\cancel{2x}}+\\cancel{2x}\\cdot \\frac{x-4}{\\cancel{2x}} & =\\cancel{2x}\\cdot \\frac{5x-6}{\\cancel{2x}} \\\\ x-2+x-4 & =5x-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now have a linear equation in $x,$ and we can solve this using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-2+x-4 & =5x-6 \\\\ 2x-6 & =5x-6 \\\\ 5x-2x & =-6+6 \\\\ 3x & =0 \\\\ x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe recall that we cannot allow $x=0$ as a solution. Therefore, we conclude that there is no solution." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c8e3c1c2-59cd-57ee-a592-7d15bb5c605d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c8e3c1c2-59cd-57ee-a592-7d15bb5c605d" :answer-field/id #uuid "c8e3c1c2-59cd-57ee-a592-7d15bb5c605d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1df39945-f17e-5051-9124-626d55bf8a1a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-64742e1b-bec8-5682-b5ee-105f5d4f7a68" "answer-abfebc27-8159-524d-9a6e-cdfd59eb0187" "answer-7532c4d0-18e0-53bb-a6b7-c9f7c5d650eb" "answer-befbf0c7-7d19-5ffd-943e-139e02963d23" "answer-1df39945-f17e-5051-9124-626d55bf8a1a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64742e1b-bec8-5682-b5ee-105f5d4f7a68" :answer/id #uuid "64742e1b-bec8-5682-b5ee-105f5d4f7a68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-abfebc27-8159-524d-9a6e-cdfd59eb0187" :answer/id #uuid "abfebc27-8159-524d-9a6e-cdfd59eb0187" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7532c4d0-18e0-53bb-a6b7-c9f7c5d650eb" :answer/id #uuid "7532c4d0-18e0-53bb-a6b7-c9f7c5d650eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-befbf0c7-7d19-5ffd-943e-139e02963d23" :answer/id #uuid "befbf0c7-7d19-5ffd-943e-139e02963d23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1df39945-f17e-5051-9124-626d55bf8a1a" :answer/id #uuid "1df39945-f17e-5051-9124-626d55bf8a1a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-21325d3f-ea32-5619-afd8-5e491ef497e5" :question/id #uuid "21325d3f-ea32-5619-afd8-5e491ef497e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-270354" :question/problem "Solve for $b$ where $\\frac{b+5}{b}+\\frac{b-7}{b}=6.$\n\n$b=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that $b=0$ is an excluded solution since division by $0$ is undefined. \n\nWe multiply both sides of the equation by $b,$ and simplify: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{b+5}{b}+\\frac{b-7}{b} & =6 \\\\ b\\cdot (\\frac{b+5}{b}+\\frac{b-7}{b}) & =b\\cdot 6 \\\\ b\\cdot \\frac{b+5}{b}+b\\cdot \\frac{b-7}{b} & =b\\cdot 6 \\\\ \\cancel{b}\\cdot \\frac{b+5}{\\cancel{b}}+\\cancel{b}\\cdot \\frac{b-7}{\\cancel{b}} & =b\\cdot 6 \\\\ b+5+b-7 & =6b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now have a linear equation in $b,$ and we can solve this using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b+5+b-7 & =6b \\\\ 2b-2 & =6b \\\\ -4b & =2 \\\\ b & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we recall that we cannot allow $b=0$ as a solution. However, since $b=-\\frac{1}{2}\\ne 0,$ we conclude that the solution is $b=-\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1e7444c8-c4e7-5947-a2ec-fcf6d2b56070"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1e7444c8-c4e7-5947-a2ec-fcf6d2b56070" :answer-field/id #uuid "1e7444c8-c4e7-5947-a2ec-fcf6d2b56070" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-c78e8f45-6241-530a-8e86-768b85aa828e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c78e8f45-6241-530a-8e86-768b85aa828e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c78e8f45-6241-530a-8e86-768b85aa828e" :answer/id #uuid "c78e8f45-6241-530a-8e86-768b85aa828e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a581df95-2d51-59ad-a71c-d2138e307e87" :question/id #uuid "a581df95-2d51-59ad-a71c-d2138e307e87" :question/math-academy-id "q-3518" :question/problem "Solve for $x$ where $\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{1}{x}=\\frac{3-x}{3x}.$" :question/worked-solution "We note that $x=0$ cannot be a solution since division by $0$ is undefined.\n\nThe equation has the denominators $x$ and $3x.$ So first, we find the least common multiple (or $\\text{LCM}$) of the denominators. We find that\n\n$$\n\\text{LCM}(x,3x)=3x.\n$$\n\nSo, we multiply both sides of the equation by $3x,$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x\\cdot (\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{1}{x}) & =3x\\cdot (\\frac{3-x}{3x}) \\\\ 3x\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}+3x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} & =3x\\cdot \\frac{3-x}{3x} \\\\ \\cancel{3}x\\cdot \\frac{2}{\\cancel{3}}+3\\cancel{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\cancel{x}} & =\\cancel{3x}\\cdot \\frac{3-x}{\\cancel{3x}} \\\\ x\\cdot (2)+3\\cdot (1) & =3-x \\\\ 2x+3 & =3-x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now have a linear equation in $x,$ and we can solve this using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+3 & =3-x \\\\ 2x+x & =3-3 \\\\ 3x & =0 \\\\ x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we recall that we cannot allow $x=0$ as a solution. Since $x=0,$ we conclude that there is no solution." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0e75216d-bcd6-569a-b621-c249dcbf26bb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0e75216d-bcd6-569a-b621-c249dcbf26bb" :answer-field/id #uuid "0e75216d-bcd6-569a-b621-c249dcbf26bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2e591bdc-0ce1-5740-b9d1-67306bc53ff7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8090692a-b362-571b-91a3-0212386b7f7c" "answer-027489bb-28e3-5dfe-a2b6-367b579e0221" "answer-2ceb2f6f-5d34-5be3-a06c-024dd0503854" "answer-fb8501be-4fcb-577e-8819-117055fdb0d2" "answer-2e591bdc-0ce1-5740-b9d1-67306bc53ff7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8090692a-b362-571b-91a3-0212386b7f7c" :answer/id #uuid "8090692a-b362-571b-91a3-0212386b7f7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-027489bb-28e3-5dfe-a2b6-367b579e0221" :answer/id #uuid "027489bb-28e3-5dfe-a2b6-367b579e0221" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ceb2f6f-5d34-5be3-a06c-024dd0503854" :answer/id #uuid "2ceb2f6f-5d34-5be3-a06c-024dd0503854" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb8501be-4fcb-577e-8819-117055fdb0d2" :answer/id #uuid "fb8501be-4fcb-577e-8819-117055fdb0d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e591bdc-0ce1-5740-b9d1-67306bc53ff7" :answer/id #uuid "2e591bdc-0ce1-5740-b9d1-67306bc53ff7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fa991cba-7607-5ad7-99b3-e6c6f2993b9f" :question/id #uuid "fa991cba-7607-5ad7-99b3-e6c6f2993b9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-115795" :question/problem "Solve for $q$ where $\\frac{2q-1}{4q}=\\frac{q+1}{3q}-1.$" :question/worked-solution "We note that $q=0$ cannot be a solution since division by $0$ is undefined. \n\nThe equation has the denominators $3q$ and $4q.$ So first, we find the least common multiple (or $\\text{LCM}$) of the denominators. We find that\n\n$$\n\\text{LCM}(3q,4q)=12q.\n$$\n\nSo, we multiply both sides of the equation by $12q,$ and simplify: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2q-1}{4q} & =\\frac{q+1}{3q}-1 \\\\ 12q\\cdot (\\frac{2q-1}{4q}) & =12q\\cdot (\\frac{q+1}{3q}-1) \\\\ 12q\\cdot \\frac{2q-1}{4q} & =12q\\cdot \\frac{q+1}{3q}-12q\\cdot 1 \\\\ 3\\cdot \\cancel{4q}\\cdot (\\frac{2q-1}{\\cancel{4q}}) & =4\\cdot \\cancel{3q}\\cdot (\\frac{q+1}{\\cancel{3q}})-12q \\\\ 3(2q-1) & =4(q+1)-12q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now have a linear equation in $q,$ and we can solve this using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(2q-1) & =4(q+1)-12q \\\\ 6q-3 & =4q+4-12q \\\\ 6q-3 & =-8q+4 \\\\ 6q+8q & =4+3 \\\\ 14q & =7 \\\\ q & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we recall that we cannot allow $q=0$ as a solution. But since $q=\\frac{1}{2}\\ne 0,$ we conclude that the solution is $q=\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9f7254ba-8516-55b4-929d-3effa926b080"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9f7254ba-8516-55b4-929d-3effa926b080" :answer-field/id #uuid "9f7254ba-8516-55b4-929d-3effa926b080" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6248e345-a77f-5d0b-a6d9-29b049db316b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dc07d439-b7d4-549a-97f7-0b5dc5b32343" "answer-2ce934f1-749e-5c82-9be2-eb4043940d41" "answer-6248e345-a77f-5d0b-a6d9-29b049db316b" "answer-b2172526-cf2e-5a91-b2a6-d166613ff60b" "answer-3fb68e51-5ee4-5bd9-86b7-657995c28427"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc07d439-b7d4-549a-97f7-0b5dc5b32343" :answer/id #uuid "dc07d439-b7d4-549a-97f7-0b5dc5b32343" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ce934f1-749e-5c82-9be2-eb4043940d41" :answer/id #uuid "2ce934f1-749e-5c82-9be2-eb4043940d41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6248e345-a77f-5d0b-a6d9-29b049db316b" :answer/id #uuid "6248e345-a77f-5d0b-a6d9-29b049db316b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2172526-cf2e-5a91-b2a6-d166613ff60b" :answer/id #uuid "b2172526-cf2e-5a91-b2a6-d166613ff60b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3fb68e51-5ee4-5bd9-86b7-657995c28427" :answer/id #uuid "3fb68e51-5ee4-5bd9-86b7-657995c28427" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f095dc29-06a2-59bf-8997-6e524951d317" :question/id #uuid "f095dc29-06a2-59bf-8997-6e524951d317" :question/math-academy-id "q-75936" :question/problem "Which value of $m$ satisfies the equation $\\frac{4m+1}{3m}-\\frac{m-1}{6m}=\\frac{1}{9m}?$" :question/worked-solution "We note that $m=0$ cannot be a solution since division by $0$ is undefined. \n\nThe equation has the denominators $3m,6m,$ and $9m.$ So first, we find the least common multiple (or $\\text{LCM}$) of the denominators. We find that\n\n$$\n\\text{LCM}(3m,6m,9m)=18m.\n$$\n\nSo, we multiply both sides of the equation by $18m,$ and simplify: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4m+1}{3m}-\\frac{m-1}{6m} & =\\frac{1}{9m} \\\\ 18m\\cdot (\\frac{4m+1}{3m}-\\frac{m-1}{6m}) & =18m\\cdot (\\frac{1}{9m}) \\\\ 18m\\cdot (\\frac{4m+1}{3m})-18m\\cdot (\\frac{m-1}{6m}) & =18m\\cdot (\\frac{1}{9m}) \\\\ 6\\cdot 3m\\cdot (\\frac{4m+1}{3m})-3\\cdot 6m\\cdot (\\frac{m-1}{6m}) & =2\\cdot 9m\\cdot (\\frac{1}{9m}) \\\\ 6\\cdot \\cancel{3m}\\cdot (\\frac{4m+1}{\\cancel{3m}})-3\\cdot \\cancel{6m}\\cdot (\\frac{m-1}{\\cancel{6m}}) & =2\\cdot \\cancel{9m}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\cancel{9m}}) \\\\ 6(4m+1)-3(m-1) & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now have a linear equation in $m,$ and we can solve this using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(4m+1)-3(m-1) & =2 \\\\ 24m+6-3m+3 & =2 \\\\ 21m+9 & =2 \\\\ 21m & =-7 \\\\ m & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we recall that we cannot allow $m=0$ as a solution. But since $m=-\\frac{1}{3}\\ne 0,$ we conclude that the solution is $m=-\\frac{1}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7b11927f-a39d-501b-8f1e-1dbd9842d17d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7b11927f-a39d-501b-8f1e-1dbd9842d17d" :answer-field/id #uuid "7b11927f-a39d-501b-8f1e-1dbd9842d17d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f109c179-6843-5d73-a8d7-5f145c4e38c7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f109c179-6843-5d73-a8d7-5f145c4e38c7" "answer-b33107cc-21e0-55e3-a66c-7183491e915e" "answer-637488d7-0f63-5fe0-8698-1d6414fe8f0c" "answer-ff7a5d0d-e5eb-5ce1-ad1a-caa3023a2a5f" "answer-173e1c1a-757c-5fcf-be6a-91e7ca4875db"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f109c179-6843-5d73-a8d7-5f145c4e38c7" :answer/id #uuid "f109c179-6843-5d73-a8d7-5f145c4e38c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b33107cc-21e0-55e3-a66c-7183491e915e" :answer/id #uuid "b33107cc-21e0-55e3-a66c-7183491e915e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-637488d7-0f63-5fe0-8698-1d6414fe8f0c" :answer/id #uuid "637488d7-0f63-5fe0-8698-1d6414fe8f0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff7a5d0d-e5eb-5ce1-ad1a-caa3023a2a5f" :answer/id #uuid "ff7a5d0d-e5eb-5ce1-ad1a-caa3023a2a5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-173e1c1a-757c-5fcf-be6a-91e7ca4875db" :answer/id #uuid "173e1c1a-757c-5fcf-be6a-91e7ca4875db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f7541a79-898f-52f6-9741-385d5ef8e2c1" :question/id #uuid "f7541a79-898f-52f6-9741-385d5ef8e2c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-75955" :question/problem "Which value of $n$ satisfies the equation $\\frac{3}{2n}-\\frac{1-n}{{n}^{2}}=\\frac{7}{3n}?$" :question/worked-solution "We note that $n=0$ cannot be a solution since division by $0$ is undefined. \n\nThe equation has the denominators $2n,$ ${n}^{2},$ and $3n.$ So first, we find the least common multiple (or $\\text{LCM}$) of the denominators. We find that\n\n$$\n\\text{LCM}(2n,{n}^{2},3n)=6{n}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, we multiply both sides of the equation by $6{n}^{2},$ and simplify: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2n}-\\frac{1-n}{{n}^{2}} & =\\frac{7}{3n} \\\\ 6{n}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{3}{2n}-\\frac{1-n}{{n}^{2}}) & =6{n}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{7}{3n}) \\\\ 6{n}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{3}{2n})-6{n}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{1-n}{{n}^{2}}) & =6{n}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{7}{3n}) \\\\ 3n\\cdot 2n\\cdot (\\frac{3}{2n})-6\\cdot {n}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{1-n}{{n}^{2}}) & =2n\\cdot 3n\\cdot (\\frac{7}{3n}) \\\\ 3n\\cdot \\cancel{2n}\\cdot (\\frac{3}{\\cancel{2n}})-6\\cdot \\cancel{{n}^{2}}\\cdot (\\frac{1-n}{\\cancel{{n}^{2}}}) & =2n\\cdot \\cancel{3n}\\cdot (\\frac{7}{\\cancel{3n}}) \\\\ 3n\\cdot (3)-6\\cdot (1-n) & =2n\\cdot (7) \\\\ 9n-6(1-n) & =14n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now have a linear equation in $n,$ and we can solve this using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9n-6(1-n) & =14n \\\\ 15n-6 & =14n \\\\ n & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we recall that we cannot allow $n=0$ as a solution. But since $n=6\\ne 0,$ we conclude that the solution is $n=6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-efc35caa-71e9-53b2-85d0-1e3c73992105"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-efc35caa-71e9-53b2-85d0-1e3c73992105" :answer-field/id #uuid "efc35caa-71e9-53b2-85d0-1e3c73992105" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2db04f8a-deb3-5e11-91d5-eea128cb749d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b61f0de4-08b9-5e89-9aaa-a012a63e7f6f" "answer-c71bf5dc-237a-5908-9987-a1df036cb19a" "answer-cf71e830-8356-5e8d-bce8-f9b93f8cc125" "answer-2db04f8a-deb3-5e11-91d5-eea128cb749d" "answer-0b7a2e99-60fa-5845-b485-7f1ecf41d0a7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b61f0de4-08b9-5e89-9aaa-a012a63e7f6f" :answer/id #uuid "b61f0de4-08b9-5e89-9aaa-a012a63e7f6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c71bf5dc-237a-5908-9987-a1df036cb19a" :answer/id #uuid "c71bf5dc-237a-5908-9987-a1df036cb19a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf71e830-8356-5e8d-bce8-f9b93f8cc125" :answer/id #uuid "cf71e830-8356-5e8d-bce8-f9b93f8cc125" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2db04f8a-deb3-5e11-91d5-eea128cb749d" :answer/id #uuid "2db04f8a-deb3-5e11-91d5-eea128cb749d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b7a2e99-60fa-5845-b485-7f1ecf41d0a7" :answer/id #uuid "0b7a2e99-60fa-5845-b485-7f1ecf41d0a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ff75b330-ecd4-5fa0-b36d-564d6c66e864" :question/id #uuid "ff75b330-ecd4-5fa0-b36d-564d6c66e864" :question/math-academy-id "q-276869" :question/problem "Solve for $v$ where $\\frac{v+4}{{v}^{2}}-\\frac{7}{6v}=\\frac{5}{2{v}^{2}}.$\n\n$v=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We note that $v=0$ cannot be a solution since division by $0$ is undefined. \n\nThe equation has the denominators $6v,\\,{v}^{2},$ and $2{v}^{2}.$ First, we find the denominators' least common multiple (or $\\text{LCM}$). We have that\n\n$$\n\\text{LCM}(6v,{v}^{2},2{v}^{2})=6{v}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, we multiply both sides of the equation by $6{v}^{2},$ and simplify: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{v+4}{{v}^{2}}-\\frac{7}{6v} & =\\frac{5}{2{v}^{2}} \\\\ 6{v}^{2}(\\frac{v+4}{{v}^{2}}-\\frac{7}{6v}) & =6{v}^{2}(\\frac{5}{2{v}^{2}}) \\\\ 6{v}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{v+4}{{v}^{2}}-6{v}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{7}{6v} & =6{v}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2{v}^{2}} \\\\ 6\\cdot {v}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{v+4}{{v}^{2}}-6v\\cdot v\\cdot \\frac{7}{6v} & =3\\cdot 2{v}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2{v}^{2}} \\\\ 6\\cdot \\cancel{{v}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{v+4}{\\cancel{{v}^{2}}}-\\cancel{6v}\\cdot v\\cdot \\frac{7}{\\cancel{6v}} & =3\\cdot \\cancel{2{v}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{5}{\\cancel{2{v}^{2}}} \\\\ 6(v+4)-v\\cdot (7) & =3\\cdot 5 \\\\ 6(v+4)-7v & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now have a linear equation in $v,$ and we can solve this using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(v+4)-7v & =15 \\\\ 6v+24-7v & =15 \\\\ -v+24 & =15 \\\\ -v & =-9 \\\\ v & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we recall that we cannot allow $v=0$ as a solution. But since $v=9\\ne 0,$ we conclude that the solution is $v=9.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-787aa0da-04c6-5397-99c2-28c45379391c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-787aa0da-04c6-5397-99c2-28c45379391c" :answer-field/id #uuid "787aa0da-04c6-5397-99c2-28c45379391c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-38875fd2-c051-51ae-9cd4-a572e31fc61c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-38875fd2-c051-51ae-9cd4-a572e31fc61c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-38875fd2-c051-51ae-9cd4-a572e31fc61c" :answer/id #uuid "38875fd2-c051-51ae-9cd4-a572e31fc61c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068969 :activity/expected-seconds 780.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133789 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cc66ebbe-2cca-5407-87bc-772df677089f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-cc66ebbe-2cca-5407-87bc-772df677089f" :question/id #uuid "cc66ebbe-2cca-5407-87bc-772df677089f" :question/math-academy-id "q-86762" :question/problem "Find the orthogonal projection of the vector $x$ onto the plane $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $v$ and $w$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSince our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}\\{v,w\\}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ v & w \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}17 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{50}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 17\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-91e225e4-0bfc-5b26-8ce8-66c5aba780de"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-91e225e4-0bfc-5b26-8ce8-66c5aba780de" :answer-field/id #uuid "91e225e4-0bfc-5b26-8ce8-66c5aba780de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cb246cd3-9bbb-53e2-b543-1ad93f9bd8ab" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0fad72e3-bee7-5eb3-9828-6bf06dfaa7af" "answer-fb15ad4b-aa77-523c-bd0d-f2171314bac1" "answer-b435f2e3-4cd8-585d-954c-52f87c1f4746" "answer-f69ae65b-9be7-53cf-91f1-13dc37eb2f46" "answer-cb246cd3-9bbb-53e2-b543-1ad93f9bd8ab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0fad72e3-bee7-5eb3-9828-6bf06dfaa7af" :answer/id #uuid "0fad72e3-bee7-5eb3-9828-6bf06dfaa7af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb15ad4b-aa77-523c-bd0d-f2171314bac1" :answer/id #uuid "fb15ad4b-aa77-523c-bd0d-f2171314bac1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b435f2e3-4cd8-585d-954c-52f87c1f4746" :answer/id #uuid "b435f2e3-4cd8-585d-954c-52f87c1f4746" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f69ae65b-9be7-53cf-91f1-13dc37eb2f46" :answer/id #uuid "f69ae65b-9be7-53cf-91f1-13dc37eb2f46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb246cd3-9bbb-53e2-b543-1ad93f9bd8ab" :answer/id #uuid "cb246cd3-9bbb-53e2-b543-1ad93f9bd8ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133788 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3a6241f6-827e-5f45-a2f2-3047ca1b82e0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-3a6241f6-827e-5f45-a2f2-3047ca1b82e0" :question/id #uuid "3a6241f6-827e-5f45-a2f2-3047ca1b82e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-86769" :question/problem "Find the vector in the subspace spanned by $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ \nthat is closest to the vector $x,$ where \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe closest vector to $x$ in the subspace spanned by $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace, which is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⇒\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}18 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-48 \\\\ 17\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{38}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 18\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-48 \\\\ 17\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9313c766-b074-562e-915b-c0a2bae81c97"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9313c766-b074-562e-915b-c0a2bae81c97" :answer-field/id #uuid "9313c766-b074-562e-915b-c0a2bae81c97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-46d8d0ee-ed43-5b82-b677-585c48864035" :answer-field/choices ["answer-94896345-dcbf-5311-af2f-0470b2af33bc" "answer-46d8d0ee-ed43-5b82-b677-585c48864035" "answer-b91ee488-df0e-59db-a257-d1dabeda41e0" "answer-b31e0d65-4eac-54bf-b80e-d663776fb997" "answer-3e5a2d37-c4d6-5c27-bc7b-4ea71231b6a8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94896345-dcbf-5311-af2f-0470b2af33bc" :answer/id #uuid "94896345-dcbf-5311-af2f-0470b2af33bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46d8d0ee-ed43-5b82-b677-585c48864035" :answer/id #uuid "46d8d0ee-ed43-5b82-b677-585c48864035" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b91ee488-df0e-59db-a257-d1dabeda41e0" :answer/id #uuid "b91ee488-df0e-59db-a257-d1dabeda41e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b31e0d65-4eac-54bf-b80e-d663776fb997" :answer/id #uuid "b31e0d65-4eac-54bf-b80e-d663776fb997" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e5a2d37-c4d6-5c27-bc7b-4ea71231b6a8" :answer/id #uuid "3e5a2d37-c4d6-5c27-bc7b-4ea71231b6a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-e25488af-2216-5d14-88af-1924c26a6fe6" :activity/id #uuid "e25488af-2216-5d14-88af-1924c26a6fe6" :activity/title "Projecting Vectors Onto Subspaces in Euclidean Spaces (Arbitrary Bases)" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049970 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-8a025179-4153-59ae-829a-43edf5b908e1" "step-c41a8537-e103-57cd-982b-440dde37abd4" "step-06674b92-79e6-5824-abba-71763f29a6cc" "step-c461e720-e126-50ff-b3e3-49b8487aab6f" "step-91f96d99-dd00-555d-a4bd-d5b4d415820a"] :activity/first-step "step-8a025179-4153-59ae-829a-43edf5b908e1" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-8a025179-4153-59ae-829a-43edf5b908e1" :step/id #uuid "8a025179-4153-59ae-829a-43edf5b908e1" :step/content 17592186392354 :step/next "step-c41a8537-e103-57cd-982b-440dde37abd4" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c41a8537-e103-57cd-982b-440dde37abd4" :step/id #uuid "c41a8537-e103-57cd-982b-440dde37abd4" :step/content "question-cc66ebbe-2cca-5407-87bc-772df677089f" :step/next "step-06674b92-79e6-5824-abba-71763f29a6cc" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-06674b92-79e6-5824-abba-71763f29a6cc" :step/id #uuid "06674b92-79e6-5824-abba-71763f29a6cc" :step/content "question-3a6241f6-827e-5f45-a2f2-3047ca1b82e0" :step/next "step-c461e720-e126-50ff-b3e3-49b8487aab6f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c461e720-e126-50ff-b3e3-49b8487aab6f" :step/id #uuid "c461e720-e126-50ff-b3e3-49b8487aab6f" :step/content 17592186365003 :step/next "step-91f96d99-dd00-555d-a4bd-d5b4d415820a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-91f96d99-dd00-555d-a4bd-d5b4d415820a" :step/id #uuid "91f96d99-dd00-555d-a4bd-d5b4d415820a" :step/content 17592186365171 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186165656 :answer-field/choices 17592186165657] [:db/retract 17592186165656 :answer-field/choices 17592186165658] [:db/retract 17592186165656 :answer-field/choices 17592186165659] [:db/retract 17592186165656 :answer-field/choices 17592186165660] [:db/retract 17592186165656 :answer-field/choices 17592186165661] {:db/id 17592186166795 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-007da683-6a06-5103-8ccf-d7e5e491284b" "question-6bf4783e-de85-5ad3-95bc-1eadaee336f8" "question-347de47e-5245-5fd2-b46a-2d80ee9ca643" "question-032608f7-6edc-5183-bb2d-4ede3e9c1645"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166633 :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nCalculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\dfrac{1}{1+\\sinh^2 x} \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity \n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x + \\sin^2 x= 1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n\\cosh^2x -\\sinh^2x=1\n$$\n\nwhich we can write as\n\n$$\n1+\\sinh^2x=\\cosh^2x.\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we have\n\n$$\n\\sech x = \\dfrac{1}{\\cosh x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x})}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sech}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166796 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a49f44d3-1abb-5067-966c-70ae50d2155e" "question-9ddcb9f3-50a1-505b-ae57-c8a55dc1f652" "question-6c61796b-b24c-5403-8a9e-cd8bda63e7c0" "question-7461b1f3-1aea-5d09-ab06-c9f25cb75e4f" "question-4e26e540-b6e1-55b9-88da-a99de2917513"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166634 :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{\\ln 2} \\dfrac{\\tanh{x}-\\tanh^3{x}}{\\sech{x}} \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the secant-tangent identity \n\n$$\n1 + \\tan^2 x= \\sec^2{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic secant-tangent identity\n\n$$\n1-\\tanh^2x=\\sech^2{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x-{tanh}^{3}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{(1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x)\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{{sech}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sech}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)+\\operatorname{sech}⁡0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}+\\frac{2}{{e}^{0}+{e}^{0}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{(2+\\frac{1}{2})}+1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{(\\frac{5}{2})}+1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166797 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-36b4a778-aa5a-54d9-9b61-eb9431bef188" "question-d50512b3-2d0b-53b0-a169-ed8ad3f44908" "question-70e33acb-bebf-51b2-9607-6c52a3430a18" "question-fe6b40d3-8971-55c8-aabc-4ac03f347ec4" "question-9ea30f92-f367-5355-89e8-50b8c17d0449"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166635 :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{\\ln 3}^{\\ln 6} \\dfrac{\\csch{x}}{\\coth^2{x} - 1} \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the cosecant-cotangent identity \n\n$$\n\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n1 + \\cot^2 x= \\csc^2{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic cosecant-cotangent identity\n\n$$\n\\coth^2x - 1=\\csch^2{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int_{\\ln 3}^{\\ln 6} \\dfrac{\\csch{x}}{\\coth^2{x} - 1} \\, \\textrm{d}x\n\t\t\t&= \\int_{\\ln 3}^{\\ln 6} \\dfrac{\\csch{x}}{\\csch^2{x}} \\, \\textrm{d}x \\[5pt]\n\t\t\t&= \\int_{\\ln 3}^{\\ln 6} \\sinh{x} \\, \\textrm{d}x \\[5pt]\n\t\t\t&= \\cosh{x} \\Big|_{\\ln 3}^{\\ln 6}\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t&= \\cosh(\\ln 6) - \\cosh(\\ln 3)\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t&= \\left(\\dfrac{e^{\\ln 6}+e^{-\\ln 6}}{2}\\right) - \\left(\\dfrac{e^{\\ln 3}+e^{-\\ln 3}}{2}\\right)\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t&= \\left(\\dfrac{6 + \\dfrac{1}{6}}{2}\\right) - \\left(\\dfrac{3 + \\dfrac{1}{3}}{2}\\right)\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t&= \\dfrac{37}{12} - \\dfrac{5}{3}\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t&= \\dfrac{37}{12} - \\dfrac{20}{12} \\[5pt]\n            &= \\dfrac{17}{12}\n\t}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166798 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c7a3ee0b-1bd5-5d07-b45d-54312bc57611" "question-f321e82d-23c7-5f15-828b-dbb232e439d7" "question-7649fd25-c8c5-5938-a768-41b9d4f9aa06" "question-1c959d7c-d68c-591a-a3b7-ea71063de12e" "question-56c765b2-a04b-54c3-b2ad-79e20147ade9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166636 :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int \\dfrac{2}{\\cosh^2(2x+1)-1} \\, \\textrm{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 \\theta + \\sin^2 \\theta = 1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n\\cosh^2 \\theta - \\sinh^2 \\theta = 1.\n$$\n\nSetting $\\theta = 2x + 1,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\cosh^2 (2x+1) - \\sinh^2(2x+1) = 1\n$$\n\nwhich can be written as\n\n$$\n\\cosh^2 (2x+1) -1 = \\sinh^2(2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{{cosh}^{2}⁡(2x+1)-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int {csch}^{2}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{coth}⁡(2x+1)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-007da683-6a06-5103-8ccf-d7e5e491284b" :question/id #uuid "007da683-6a06-5103-8ccf-d7e5e491284b" :question/math-academy-id "q-96324" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{1-{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity \n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite and calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{1-(1+{sinh}^{2}⁡x)}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\int \\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\int {csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-588c50be-27c2-58c4-af3b-6c4e820c32d8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-588c50be-27c2-58c4-af3b-6c4e820c32d8" :answer-field/id #uuid "588c50be-27c2-58c4-af3b-6c4e820c32d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-03d5f670-27f0-5761-9a2d-2b27183ed602" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6f28b0d3-c0bf-5fe7-bb38-6f7358465bb5" "answer-ed5c2a17-7497-5332-bf7f-3b0c44e70ca7" "answer-03d5f670-27f0-5761-9a2d-2b27183ed602" "answer-a5a81b59-7130-5b2b-ab0f-bb39e54adc0f" "answer-475499d3-6def-57f9-991e-f031b8de6556"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f28b0d3-c0bf-5fe7-bb38-6f7358465bb5" :answer/id #uuid "6f28b0d3-c0bf-5fe7-bb38-6f7358465bb5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ed5c2a17-7497-5332-bf7f-3b0c44e70ca7" :answer/id #uuid "ed5c2a17-7497-5332-bf7f-3b0c44e70ca7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03d5f670-27f0-5761-9a2d-2b27183ed602" :answer/id #uuid "03d5f670-27f0-5761-9a2d-2b27183ed602" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5a81b59-7130-5b2b-ab0f-bb39e54adc0f" :answer/id #uuid "a5a81b59-7130-5b2b-ab0f-bb39e54adc0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-475499d3-6def-57f9-991e-f031b8de6556" :answer/id #uuid "475499d3-6def-57f9-991e-f031b8de6556" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6bf4783e-de85-5ad3-95bc-1eadaee336f8" :question/id #uuid "6bf4783e-de85-5ad3-95bc-1eadaee336f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-96307" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int (1-{sinh}^{2}⁡x{sech}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity \n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sech}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (1-{sinh}^{2}⁡x{sech}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1-{sinh}^{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sech}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-215a951f-a6c0-593d-8a1c-917970be4ccd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-215a951f-a6c0-593d-8a1c-917970be4ccd" :answer-field/id #uuid "215a951f-a6c0-593d-8a1c-917970be4ccd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1734e68b-49b7-5657-a8ab-e7fd14ec92c1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b0bcfa39-281d-566a-8e63-d65c56907c98" "answer-e4a99a7f-7e6c-5818-a83d-a13f8c260bfa" "answer-1734e68b-49b7-5657-a8ab-e7fd14ec92c1" "answer-faef0ce8-c4e4-53a3-9255-f04524119f87" "answer-6de2d048-caee-5e8a-baf6-c37fde229e82"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b0bcfa39-281d-566a-8e63-d65c56907c98" :answer/id #uuid "b0bcfa39-281d-566a-8e63-d65c56907c98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4a99a7f-7e6c-5818-a83d-a13f8c260bfa" :answer/id #uuid "e4a99a7f-7e6c-5818-a83d-a13f8c260bfa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1734e68b-49b7-5657-a8ab-e7fd14ec92c1" :answer/id #uuid "1734e68b-49b7-5657-a8ab-e7fd14ec92c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-faef0ce8-c4e4-53a3-9255-f04524119f87" :answer/id #uuid "faef0ce8-c4e4-53a3-9255-f04524119f87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6de2d048-caee-5e8a-baf6-c37fde229e82" :answer/id #uuid "6de2d048-caee-5e8a-baf6-c37fde229e82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-347de47e-5245-5fd2-b46a-2d80ee9ca643" :question/id #uuid "347de47e-5245-5fd2-b46a-2d80ee9ca643" :question/math-academy-id "q-165872" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x+{sinh}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity \n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite and calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x+{sinh}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x(1+{sinh}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bef0a448-ccbc-545d-a9c9-133e5c77b5fa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bef0a448-ccbc-545d-a9c9-133e5c77b5fa" :answer-field/id #uuid "bef0a448-ccbc-545d-a9c9-133e5c77b5fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2a908713-5ac5-5134-a0e7-86afc9750420" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2a908713-5ac5-5134-a0e7-86afc9750420" "answer-fedaa517-46ad-50d1-9223-915aeb1842d4" "answer-d67bbc9b-a120-5ae6-be39-d2884fe54ab0" "answer-4f3c99bb-9d3b-5885-8411-3a5f94462ecf" "answer-7ac49e22-956a-5757-b843-898b336ff080"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a908713-5ac5-5134-a0e7-86afc9750420" :answer/id #uuid "2a908713-5ac5-5134-a0e7-86afc9750420" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fedaa517-46ad-50d1-9223-915aeb1842d4" :answer/id #uuid "fedaa517-46ad-50d1-9223-915aeb1842d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d67bbc9b-a120-5ae6-be39-d2884fe54ab0" :answer/id #uuid "d67bbc9b-a120-5ae6-be39-d2884fe54ab0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f3c99bb-9d3b-5885-8411-3a5f94462ecf" :answer/id #uuid "4f3c99bb-9d3b-5885-8411-3a5f94462ecf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ac49e22-956a-5757-b843-898b336ff080" :answer/id #uuid "7ac49e22-956a-5757-b843-898b336ff080" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-032608f7-6edc-5183-bb2d-4ede3e9c1645" :question/id #uuid "032608f7-6edc-5183-bb2d-4ede3e9c1645" :question/math-academy-id "q-96306" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int ({cosh}^{3}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity \n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({cosh}^{3}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cosh}⁡x({cosh}^{2}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-81975dcf-378c-5d3d-b3d0-17574131c4e8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-81975dcf-378c-5d3d-b3d0-17574131c4e8" :answer-field/id #uuid "81975dcf-378c-5d3d-b3d0-17574131c4e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-98505c70-07f9-5bd5-816f-3af8a4adc0d6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-928181c8-6764-5052-ab91-3e3d8b3ae162" "answer-187fa676-ce69-5db4-bb19-2d5aded139fe" "answer-3170b4a1-795f-56db-b544-2a4162816f46" "answer-98505c70-07f9-5bd5-816f-3af8a4adc0d6" "answer-a2148279-dc40-5ab9-8eaa-86cdbddf62fd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-928181c8-6764-5052-ab91-3e3d8b3ae162" :answer/id #uuid "928181c8-6764-5052-ab91-3e3d8b3ae162" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-187fa676-ce69-5db4-bb19-2d5aded139fe" :answer/id #uuid "187fa676-ce69-5db4-bb19-2d5aded139fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3170b4a1-795f-56db-b544-2a4162816f46" :answer/id #uuid "3170b4a1-795f-56db-b544-2a4162816f46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-98505c70-07f9-5bd5-816f-3af8a4adc0d6" :answer/id #uuid "98505c70-07f9-5bd5-816f-3af8a4adc0d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2148279-dc40-5ab9-8eaa-86cdbddf62fd" :answer/id #uuid "a2148279-dc40-5ab9-8eaa-86cdbddf62fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167408 :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{coth}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity \n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{coth}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{coth}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{{coth}^{2}⁡x}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x-1+1}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{{coth}^{2}⁡x}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{(\\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x})}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186165656 :answer-field/correct "answer-744490d1-9896-5ac5-9b5a-97aeb15a3238" :answer-field/choices ["answer-744490d1-9896-5ac5-9b5a-97aeb15a3238" "answer-421b7a92-fb82-5fac-b1cf-0b831b760fd1" "answer-84be6896-bcea-56cf-8b32-6d72991af814" "answer-94e81827-f57f-549f-8221-d7c1a9b3c0c3" "answer-cc34c6ea-57ba-59bc-8e55-253f0cdf1126"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-744490d1-9896-5ac5-9b5a-97aeb15a3238" :answer/id #uuid "744490d1-9896-5ac5-9b5a-97aeb15a3238" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-421b7a92-fb82-5fac-b1cf-0b831b760fd1" :answer/id #uuid "421b7a92-fb82-5fac-b1cf-0b831b760fd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84be6896-bcea-56cf-8b32-6d72991af814" :answer/id #uuid "84be6896-bcea-56cf-8b32-6d72991af814" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94e81827-f57f-549f-8221-d7c1a9b3c0c3" :answer/id #uuid "94e81827-f57f-549f-8221-d7c1a9b3c0c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc34c6ea-57ba-59bc-8e55-253f0cdf1126" :answer/id #uuid "cc34c6ea-57ba-59bc-8e55-253f0cdf1126" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sech}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a49f44d3-1abb-5067-966c-70ae50d2155e" :question/id #uuid "a49f44d3-1abb-5067-966c-70ae50d2155e" :question/math-academy-id "q-96429" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{2-2{tanh}^{4}⁡x}{1+{tanh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the secant-tangent identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic secant-tangent identity\n\n$$\n1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x={sech}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{2-2{tanh}^{4}⁡x}{1+{tanh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{1-{tanh}^{4}⁡x}{1+{tanh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{(1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x)(1+{tanh}^{2}⁡x)}{1+{tanh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{sech}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)-2\\operatorname{tanh}⁡0 \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+1}-2\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{0}-1}{{e}^{0}+1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{2}^{2}-1}{{2}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-58f1aa97-2aa4-5f57-8fa7-34a54ff2bfe8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-58f1aa97-2aa4-5f57-8fa7-34a54ff2bfe8" :answer-field/id #uuid "58f1aa97-2aa4-5f57-8fa7-34a54ff2bfe8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2efeda09-6488-58c8-b51d-5cb115113e8b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bd388afb-e318-5bb0-ad11-815dec250e03" "answer-3694787f-4267-5b85-9a9d-c811b7ca8c3f" "answer-5c2f505b-06f8-527d-b1b4-f411adee504d" "answer-ee6a0a2b-3a0c-5024-a882-d244026f8d60" "answer-2efeda09-6488-58c8-b51d-5cb115113e8b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd388afb-e318-5bb0-ad11-815dec250e03" :answer/id #uuid "bd388afb-e318-5bb0-ad11-815dec250e03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3694787f-4267-5b85-9a9d-c811b7ca8c3f" :answer/id #uuid "3694787f-4267-5b85-9a9d-c811b7ca8c3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c2f505b-06f8-527d-b1b4-f411adee504d" :answer/id #uuid "5c2f505b-06f8-527d-b1b4-f411adee504d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee6a0a2b-3a0c-5024-a882-d244026f8d60" :answer/id #uuid "ee6a0a2b-3a0c-5024-a882-d244026f8d60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2efeda09-6488-58c8-b51d-5cb115113e8b" :answer/id #uuid "2efeda09-6488-58c8-b51d-5cb115113e8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9ddcb9f3-50a1-505b-ae57-c8a55dc1f652" :question/id #uuid "9ddcb9f3-50a1-505b-ae57-c8a55dc1f652" :question/math-academy-id "q-347992" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{{sech}^{2}⁡x}{1-{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the secant-tangent identity \n\n$$\n{sec}^{2}⁡x-1={tan}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic secant-tangent identity\n\n$$\n1-{sech}^{2}⁡x={tanh}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{{sech}^{2}⁡x}{1-{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{{sech}^{2}⁡x}{{tanh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{sech}^{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{tanh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x{|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)-\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)-\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}-\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+{2}^{-1}}{2-{2}^{-1}}-\\frac{4+{4}^{-1}}{4-{4}^{-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}-\\frac{17}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6cecfe57-733c-5892-b9ce-085b5206a4dd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6cecfe57-733c-5892-b9ce-085b5206a4dd" :answer-field/id #uuid "6cecfe57-733c-5892-b9ce-085b5206a4dd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-5ba324a1-6779-572b-99bc-3815b4a02bbf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5ba324a1-6779-572b-99bc-3815b4a02bbf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ba324a1-6779-572b-99bc-3815b4a02bbf" :answer/id #uuid "5ba324a1-6779-572b-99bc-3815b4a02bbf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6c61796b-b24c-5403-8a9e-cd8bda63e7c0" :question/id #uuid "6c61796b-b24c-5403-8a9e-cd8bda63e7c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-96405" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x(1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the secant-tangent identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic secant-tangent identity\n\n$$\n1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x={sech}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x(1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡(1-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cosh}⁡x(1-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cosh}⁡x(1-\\frac{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b7f36f1c-baeb-5d0c-a838-31d70af0c742"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b7f36f1c-baeb-5d0c-a838-31d70af0c742" :answer-field/id #uuid "b7f36f1c-baeb-5d0c-a838-31d70af0c742" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-71d70417-7ef2-5fec-908e-11a78c840b3d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a5f2dbd6-7b66-5d4d-b301-a9bd61a52a63" "answer-0035feb3-cb79-5047-8afd-04eee047fe8f" "answer-37efae25-c6d0-510f-8a84-02b69180da3f" "answer-e4fc32da-9081-513c-b08e-78ad9623f9b9" "answer-71d70417-7ef2-5fec-908e-11a78c840b3d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5f2dbd6-7b66-5d4d-b301-a9bd61a52a63" :answer/id #uuid "a5f2dbd6-7b66-5d4d-b301-a9bd61a52a63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0035feb3-cb79-5047-8afd-04eee047fe8f" :answer/id #uuid "0035feb3-cb79-5047-8afd-04eee047fe8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{csch}⁡x-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-37efae25-c6d0-510f-8a84-02b69180da3f" :answer/id #uuid "37efae25-c6d0-510f-8a84-02b69180da3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4fc32da-9081-513c-b08e-78ad9623f9b9" :answer/id #uuid "e4fc32da-9081-513c-b08e-78ad9623f9b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x+\\operatorname{sech}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-71d70417-7ef2-5fec-908e-11a78c840b3d" :answer/id #uuid "71d70417-7ef2-5fec-908e-11a78c840b3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7461b1f3-1aea-5d09-ab06-c9f25cb75e4f" :question/id #uuid "7461b1f3-1aea-5d09-ab06-c9f25cb75e4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-348024" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{8\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-8\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x{tanh}^{2}⁡x}{{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the secant-tangent identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic secant-tangent identity\n\n$$\n1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x={sech}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{8\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-8\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x{tanh}^{2}⁡x}{{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{8\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\cdot (1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x)}{{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{8\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\cdot {sech}^{2}⁡x}{{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}8\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x{|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =8(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡0) \\\\  & =8(\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{0}+{e}^{-(0)}}{2}) \\\\  & =8(\\frac{2+{2}^{-1}}{2}-1) \\\\  & =8(\\frac{5}{4}-1) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-52fbaaa5-e6e2-563a-8fc8-919869cd64cf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-52fbaaa5-e6e2-563a-8fc8-919869cd64cf" :answer-field/id #uuid "52fbaaa5-e6e2-563a-8fc8-919869cd64cf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-620344d8-2da9-55c3-b8ec-d1845745c666" :answer-field/choices ["answer-620344d8-2da9-55c3-b8ec-d1845745c666"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-620344d8-2da9-55c3-b8ec-d1845745c666" :answer/id #uuid "620344d8-2da9-55c3-b8ec-d1845745c666" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4e26e540-b6e1-55b9-88da-a99de2917513" :question/id #uuid "4e26e540-b6e1-55b9-88da-a99de2917513" :question/math-academy-id "q-96413" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{{sech}^{2}⁡x}{1-{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the secant-tangent identity \n\n$$\n{sec}^{2}⁡x-1={tan}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic secant-tangent identity\n\n$$\n1-{sech}^{2}⁡x={tanh}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{{sech}^{2}⁡x}{1-{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{{sech}^{2}⁡x}{{tanh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)+\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-1}+\\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{3}^{2}+1}{{3}^{2}-1}+\\frac{{2}^{2}+1}{{2}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}+\\frac{5}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-99b9d7f0-5aa1-5376-9c8e-7d9cbe16f0be"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-99b9d7f0-5aa1-5376-9c8e-7d9cbe16f0be" :answer-field/id #uuid "99b9d7f0-5aa1-5376-9c8e-7d9cbe16f0be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7bfe03f4-86e8-5f5d-a0ca-5eb20dd2e305" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ce716d8d-6f47-5a0f-9225-7a0aa1742627" "answer-7178716b-d298-5054-a295-621e46c31b5c" "answer-7bfe03f4-86e8-5f5d-a0ca-5eb20dd2e305" "answer-24173e0a-d957-5f97-a5dc-7d867846fe63" "answer-c4de1550-9555-521c-8641-82bf296c4387"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce716d8d-6f47-5a0f-9225-7a0aa1742627" :answer/id #uuid "ce716d8d-6f47-5a0f-9225-7a0aa1742627" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7178716b-d298-5054-a295-621e46c31b5c" :answer/id #uuid "7178716b-d298-5054-a295-621e46c31b5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7bfe03f4-86e8-5f5d-a0ca-5eb20dd2e305" :answer/id #uuid "7bfe03f4-86e8-5f5d-a0ca-5eb20dd2e305" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-24173e0a-d957-5f97-a5dc-7d867846fe63" :answer/id #uuid "24173e0a-d957-5f97-a5dc-7d867846fe63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4de1550-9555-521c-8641-82bf296c4387" :answer/id #uuid "c4de1550-9555-521c-8641-82bf296c4387" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-36b4a778-aa5a-54d9-9b61-eb9431bef188" :question/id #uuid "36b4a778-aa5a-54d9-9b61-eb9431bef188" :question/math-academy-id "q-96435" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{{coth}^{4}⁡x-1}{1+{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the cosecant-cotangent identity \n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic cosecant-cotangent identity\n\n$$\n{coth}^{2}⁡x-1={csch}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{{coth}^{4}⁡x-1}{1+{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{({coth}^{2}⁡x-1)({coth}^{2}⁡x+1)}{1+{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}({coth}^{2}⁡x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)+\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-1}+\\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{17}{15}+\\frac{5}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{60}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6903f8c0-f369-5cc9-83aa-7a2303f7c793"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6903f8c0-f369-5cc9-83aa-7a2303f7c793" :answer-field/id #uuid "6903f8c0-f369-5cc9-83aa-7a2303f7c793" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bb7393b4-08fb-5fb1-83f1-d004cc94717c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9e310136-b483-5416-b6c1-753bd73f9e7f" "answer-1f919a0d-34cf-5c87-9355-e889ab85f2d3" "answer-9807cc06-0ffd-5b61-ad8a-0beb97bc28e6" "answer-a02ac5b9-33ba-5281-baef-70b3880d7010" "answer-bb7393b4-08fb-5fb1-83f1-d004cc94717c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9e310136-b483-5416-b6c1-753bd73f9e7f" :answer/id #uuid "9e310136-b483-5416-b6c1-753bd73f9e7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{32}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f919a0d-34cf-5c87-9355-e889ab85f2d3" :answer/id #uuid "1f919a0d-34cf-5c87-9355-e889ab85f2d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{17}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9807cc06-0ffd-5b61-ad8a-0beb97bc28e6" :answer/id #uuid "9807cc06-0ffd-5b61-ad8a-0beb97bc28e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{32}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a02ac5b9-33ba-5281-baef-70b3880d7010" :answer/id #uuid "a02ac5b9-33ba-5281-baef-70b3880d7010" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bb7393b4-08fb-5fb1-83f1-d004cc94717c" :answer/id #uuid "bb7393b4-08fb-5fb1-83f1-d004cc94717c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{60}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d50512b3-2d0b-53b0-a169-ed8ad3f44908" :question/id #uuid "d50512b3-2d0b-53b0-a169-ed8ad3f44908" :question/math-academy-id "q-348041" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}\\frac{1+{csch}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡x{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the cotangent-cosecant identity \n\n$$\n{csc}^{2}⁡x-1={cot}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic identity\n\n$$\n1+{csch}^{2}⁡x={coth}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}\\frac{1+{csch}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡x{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}\\frac{{coth}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡x{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x{|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡8)-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8-{8}^{-1}}{2}-\\frac{2-{2}^{-1}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{63}{16}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{51}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fb58dffd-ddd5-56a7-b417-3fbe9d0a8b25"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fb58dffd-ddd5-56a7-b417-3fbe9d0a8b25" :answer-field/id #uuid "fb58dffd-ddd5-56a7-b417-3fbe9d0a8b25" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-2b3cfb59-acb3-5458-a2b9-9970c1414d6b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2b3cfb59-acb3-5458-a2b9-9970c1414d6b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b3cfb59-acb3-5458-a2b9-9970c1414d6b" :answer/id #uuid "2b3cfb59-acb3-5458-a2b9-9970c1414d6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{51}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-70e33acb-bebf-51b2-9607-6c52a3430a18" :question/id #uuid "70e33acb-bebf-51b2-9607-6c52a3430a18" :question/math-academy-id "q-362032" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{2}^{7}\\frac{{coth}^{4}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,{coth}^{2}⁡x}{{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the cotangent-cosecant identity \n\n$$\n{csc}^{2}⁡x-1={cot}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic identity\n\n$$\n{coth}^{2}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{7}\\frac{{coth}^{4}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,{coth}^{2}⁡x}{{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{2}^{7}\\frac{{coth}^{2}⁡x({coth}^{2}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x)}{{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{7}({coth}^{2}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{7}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{|}_{2}^{7} \\\\  & =7-2 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-db4c0633-bccb-5234-a9ce-6b6aa8a3a63d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-db4c0633-bccb-5234-a9ce-6b6aa8a3a63d" :answer-field/id #uuid "db4c0633-bccb-5234-a9ce-6b6aa8a3a63d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d2d80338-bd01-53da-9ff6-138404ba74a2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d2d80338-bd01-53da-9ff6-138404ba74a2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2d80338-bd01-53da-9ff6-138404ba74a2" :answer/id #uuid "d2d80338-bd01-53da-9ff6-138404ba74a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fe6b40d3-8971-55c8-aabc-4ac03f347ec4" :question/id #uuid "fe6b40d3-8971-55c8-aabc-4ac03f347ec4" :question/math-academy-id "q-348060" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{x{coth}^{2}⁡x+x{csch}^{2}⁡x}{{coth}^{4}⁡x-{csch}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the cotangent-cosecant identity \n\n$$\n{csc}^{2}⁡x-{cot}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic identity\n\n$$\n{coth}^{2}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{x{coth}^{2}⁡x+x{csch}^{2}⁡x}{{coth}^{4}⁡x-{csch}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{x({coth}^{2}⁡x+{csch}^{2}⁡x)}{({coth}^{2}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x)({coth}^{2}⁡x+{csch}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{x}{({coth}^{2}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{x}{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-05363739-1254-5772-8cac-8bed71ed94ea"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-05363739-1254-5772-8cac-8bed71ed94ea" :answer-field/id #uuid "05363739-1254-5772-8cac-8bed71ed94ea" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-98cbc359-2b03-5efc-8078-0d38570b0f9e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-98cbc359-2b03-5efc-8078-0d38570b0f9e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-98cbc359-2b03-5efc-8078-0d38570b0f9e" :answer/id #uuid "98cbc359-2b03-5efc-8078-0d38570b0f9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9ea30f92-f367-5355-89e8-50b8c17d0449" :question/id #uuid "9ea30f92-f367-5355-89e8-50b8c17d0449" :question/math-academy-id "q-348034" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+{csch}^{3}⁡x}{\\operatorname{coth}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the cotangent-cosecant identity \n\n$$\n{csc}^{2}⁡x-1={cot}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic identity\n\n$$\n1+{csch}^{2}⁡x={coth}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+{csch}^{3}⁡x}{\\operatorname{coth}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(1+{csch}^{2}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{coth}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\cdot {coth}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{coth}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x{|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{csch}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)-\\operatorname{csch}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csch}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)-\\operatorname{csch}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}-\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2-{2}^{-1}}-\\frac{2}{3-{3}^{-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cc85decb-7916-5052-8222-edcbe0f6343d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cc85decb-7916-5052-8222-edcbe0f6343d" :answer-field/id #uuid "cc85decb-7916-5052-8222-edcbe0f6343d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-59b81cdd-3fb5-51c1-a54c-615d09c8f887" :answer-field/choices ["answer-59b81cdd-3fb5-51c1-a54c-615d09c8f887"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-59b81cdd-3fb5-51c1-a54c-615d09c8f887" :answer/id #uuid "59b81cdd-3fb5-51c1-a54c-615d09c8f887" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c7a3ee0b-1bd5-5d07-b45d-54312bc57611" :question/id #uuid "c7a3ee0b-1bd5-5d07-b45d-54312bc57611" :question/math-academy-id "q-165895" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{6}{1+{sinh}^{2}⁡(3x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sinh}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\n$$\n\nSetting $\\theta =3x+2,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cosh}^{2}⁡(3x+2)-{sinh}^{2}⁡(3x+2) & =1 \\\\ 1+{sinh}^{2}⁡(3x+2) & ={cosh}^{2}⁡(3x+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{6}{1+{sinh}^{2}⁡(3x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{6}{{cosh}^{2}⁡(3x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int \\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡(3x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int {sech}^{2}⁡(3x+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(3x+2)+C \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(3x+2)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-64a7f0e3-b811-5999-abd0-ca813f824353"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-64a7f0e3-b811-5999-abd0-ca813f824353" :answer-field/id #uuid "64a7f0e3-b811-5999-abd0-ca813f824353" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e53abd82-d6d2-5619-b674-b500de889e2a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e4d1307c-5521-5cc2-9ba5-b15d1d2d5bdd" "answer-e53abd82-d6d2-5619-b674-b500de889e2a" "answer-9742393d-a500-5c2a-8afe-aa9646453e0c" "answer-efcebe4a-a0df-535b-8f64-7bd2e11ab057" "answer-bf467dbf-ef4a-570d-9381-8136807b7ed0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4d1307c-5521-5cc2-9ba5-b15d1d2d5bdd" :answer/id #uuid "e4d1307c-5521-5cc2-9ba5-b15d1d2d5bdd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sech}⁡(3x+2)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e53abd82-d6d2-5619-b674-b500de889e2a" :answer/id #uuid "e53abd82-d6d2-5619-b674-b500de889e2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(3x+2)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9742393d-a500-5c2a-8afe-aa9646453e0c" :answer/id #uuid "9742393d-a500-5c2a-8afe-aa9646453e0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(3x+2)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-efcebe4a-a0df-535b-8f64-7bd2e11ab057" :answer/id #uuid "efcebe4a-a0df-535b-8f64-7bd2e11ab057" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\operatorname{sech}⁡(3x+2)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bf467dbf-ef4a-570d-9381-8136807b7ed0" :answer/id #uuid "bf467dbf-ef4a-570d-9381-8136807b7ed0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(3x+2)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f321e82d-23c7-5f15-828b-dbb232e439d7" :question/id #uuid "f321e82d-23c7-5f15-828b-dbb232e439d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-96522" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{csch}^{3}⁡(7x-2)+\\operatorname{csch}⁡(7x-2)}{\\operatorname{coth}⁡(7x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the cosecant-cotangent identity \n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic cosecant-cotangent identity\n\n$$\n{coth}^{2}⁡\\theta -1={csch}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nSetting $\\theta =7x-2,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{coth}^{2}⁡(7x-2)-1 & ={csch}^{2}⁡(7x-2) \\\\ {coth}^{2}⁡(7x-2) & ={csch}^{2}⁡(7x-2)+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{csch}^{3}⁡(7x-2)+\\operatorname{csch}⁡(7x-2)}{\\operatorname{coth}⁡(7x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡(7x-2)[{csch}^{2}⁡(7x-2)+1]}{\\operatorname{coth}⁡(7x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡(7x-2){coth}^{2}⁡(7x-2)}{\\operatorname{coth}⁡(7x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{csch}⁡(7x-2)\\operatorname{coth}⁡(7x-2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{csch}⁡(7x-2)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-919f8a47-bdd5-52ef-8d35-92386471095f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-919f8a47-bdd5-52ef-8d35-92386471095f" :answer-field/id #uuid "919f8a47-bdd5-52ef-8d35-92386471095f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dd74e5e2-9f80-5316-85b3-b0b8a53ad347" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dd74e5e2-9f80-5316-85b3-b0b8a53ad347" "answer-a9b368e1-f7b0-5dd8-92cb-a1654e1ce507" "answer-d97a0c7a-a10a-50ef-8a0c-e16fb5ef9b78" "answer-7dc7a7fb-89cd-51cd-aab3-8e7b474b89ac" "answer-f46ac096-0fba-5cb8-8f28-45008d53cdf0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd74e5e2-9f80-5316-85b3-b0b8a53ad347" :answer/id #uuid "dd74e5e2-9f80-5316-85b3-b0b8a53ad347" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{csch}⁡(7x-2)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9b368e1-f7b0-5dd8-92cb-a1654e1ce507" :answer/id #uuid "a9b368e1-f7b0-5dd8-92cb-a1654e1ce507" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{coth}⁡(7x-2)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d97a0c7a-a10a-50ef-8a0c-e16fb5ef9b78" :answer/id #uuid "d97a0c7a-a10a-50ef-8a0c-e16fb5ef9b78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{csch}⁡(7x-2)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7dc7a7fb-89cd-51cd-aab3-8e7b474b89ac" :answer/id #uuid "7dc7a7fb-89cd-51cd-aab3-8e7b474b89ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{coth}⁡(7x-2)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f46ac096-0fba-5cb8-8f28-45008d53cdf0" :answer/id #uuid "f46ac096-0fba-5cb8-8f28-45008d53cdf0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{csch}⁡(7x-2)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7649fd25-c8c5-5938-a768-41b9d4f9aa06" :question/id #uuid "7649fd25-c8c5-5938-a768-41b9d4f9aa06" :question/math-academy-id "q-96453" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{cosh}^{3}⁡(2x-1)}{1+{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x-1)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sinh}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\n$$\n\nSetting $\\theta =2x-1,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cosh}^{2}⁡(2x-1)-{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x-1) & =1 \\\\ {cosh}^{2}⁡(2x-1) & =1+{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{cosh}^{3}⁡(2x-1)}{1+{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x-1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{{cosh}^{3}⁡(2x-1)}{{cosh}^{2}⁡(2x-1)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x-1)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-571ff74d-f457-5675-971d-04ff30533fde"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-571ff74d-f457-5675-971d-04ff30533fde" :answer-field/id #uuid "571ff74d-f457-5675-971d-04ff30533fde" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-185f59eb-c2e7-5a3f-a3b7-be2964f06456" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f153bba0-8285-5094-83d7-3b533736f1b1" "answer-4d024158-1b7c-5e9c-9ace-8dd0eea976bb" "answer-e3091fa4-afc7-563c-9eae-29ea28d513b1" "answer-ce2953bb-7aa8-5c3f-9a2d-3cafbe68e61e" "answer-185f59eb-c2e7-5a3f-a3b7-be2964f06456"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f153bba0-8285-5094-83d7-3b533736f1b1" :answer/id #uuid "f153bba0-8285-5094-83d7-3b533736f1b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x-1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d024158-1b7c-5e9c-9ace-8dd0eea976bb" :answer/id #uuid "4d024158-1b7c-5e9c-9ace-8dd0eea976bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x+1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e3091fa4-afc7-563c-9eae-29ea28d513b1" :answer/id #uuid "e3091fa4-afc7-563c-9eae-29ea28d513b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x-1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce2953bb-7aa8-5c3f-9a2d-3cafbe68e61e" :answer/id #uuid "ce2953bb-7aa8-5c3f-9a2d-3cafbe68e61e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x+1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-185f59eb-c2e7-5a3f-a3b7-be2964f06456" :answer/id #uuid "185f59eb-c2e7-5a3f-a3b7-be2964f06456" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x-1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1c959d7c-d68c-591a-a3b7-ea71063de12e" :question/id #uuid "1c959d7c-d68c-591a-a3b7-ea71063de12e" :question/math-academy-id "q-96466" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int (2{cosh}^{2}⁡(5x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})+4{x}^{3}-2{sinh}^{2}⁡(5x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}))\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sinh}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\n$$\n\nSetting $\\theta =5x-\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cosh}^{2}⁡(5x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})-{sinh}^{2}⁡(5x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2{cosh}^{2}⁡(5x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})+4{x}^{3}-2{sinh}^{2}⁡(5x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}))\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2[{cosh}^{2}⁡(5x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})-{sinh}^{2}⁡(5x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})]+4{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2+4{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 2\\cdot \\text{d}x+\\int 4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x+{x}^{4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9dacd865-577a-5c58-b803-da35ca44d6b7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9dacd865-577a-5c58-b803-da35ca44d6b7" :answer-field/id #uuid "9dacd865-577a-5c58-b803-da35ca44d6b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6d2f4d68-d3cb-5e06-9684-ade0a7155990" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d825bf38-2203-5280-977c-5f960b7c5773" "answer-6d2f4d68-d3cb-5e06-9684-ade0a7155990" "answer-14056c1d-1503-5c16-903f-a42353bc7679" "answer-cdcf0690-e390-5dbd-b7f0-70fd10a011b0" "answer-128c44ff-5002-57ad-a45f-4e742d10c24e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d825bf38-2203-5280-977c-5f960b7c5773" :answer/id #uuid "d825bf38-2203-5280-977c-5f960b7c5773" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2+{x}^{4}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d2f4d68-d3cb-5e06-9684-ade0a7155990" :answer/id #uuid "6d2f4d68-d3cb-5e06-9684-ade0a7155990" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+{x}^{4}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-14056c1d-1503-5c16-903f-a42353bc7679" :answer/id #uuid "14056c1d-1503-5c16-903f-a42353bc7679" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}^{2}+2{x}^{4}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cdcf0690-e390-5dbd-b7f0-70fd10a011b0" :answer/id #uuid "cdcf0690-e390-5dbd-b7f0-70fd10a011b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{5}+{x}^{4}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-128c44ff-5002-57ad-a45f-4e742d10c24e" :answer/id #uuid "128c44ff-5002-57ad-a45f-4e742d10c24e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}+2{x}^{4}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-56c765b2-a04b-54c3-b2ad-79e20147ade9" :question/id #uuid "56c765b2-a04b-54c3-b2ad-79e20147ade9" :question/math-academy-id "q-165894" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{2+2{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sinh}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\n$$\n\nSetting $\\theta =2x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cosh}^{2}⁡(2x)-{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x) & =1 \\\\ 1+{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x) & ={cosh}^{2}⁡(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2+2{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{2(1+{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x))}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{2{cosh}^{2}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x)+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-65a3f970-a115-5042-b8a1-b96f4f8015c0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-65a3f970-a115-5042-b8a1-b96f4f8015c0" :answer-field/id #uuid "65a3f970-a115-5042-b8a1-b96f4f8015c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-14f6e04e-fb88-5362-9549-483100fa12e2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-84b7088f-f334-521c-a837-e560bd2f92fa" "answer-d41fcdf0-a6d8-5e72-ac3e-0c3d81a914c4" "answer-2b0b4705-45a1-5421-a9c7-5785f003fa93" "answer-e3c2410b-a921-5ac6-85cf-3cff52fdee7d" "answer-14f6e04e-fb88-5362-9549-483100fa12e2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84b7088f-f334-521c-a837-e560bd2f92fa" :answer/id #uuid "84b7088f-f334-521c-a837-e560bd2f92fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d41fcdf0-a6d8-5e72-ac3e-0c3d81a914c4" :answer/id #uuid "d41fcdf0-a6d8-5e72-ac3e-0c3d81a914c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b0b4705-45a1-5421-a9c7-5785f003fa93" :answer/id #uuid "2b0b4705-45a1-5421-a9c7-5785f003fa93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e3c2410b-a921-5ac6-85cf-3cff52fdee7d" :answer/id #uuid "e3c2410b-a921-5ac6-85cf-3cff52fdee7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-14f6e04e-fb88-5362-9549-483100fa12e2" :answer/id #uuid "14f6e04e-fb88-5362-9549-483100fa12e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186168118 :tutorial/content "We can compute integrals containing hyperbolic functions using the hyperbolic counterparts of the Pythagorean identity. We use Osborn's rule to convert a trigonometric identity to a corresponding hyperbolic identity. \n\nOsborn's rule states that to convert a trigonometric identity to a corresponding hyperbolic identity, we\n\n- replace every trigonometric function with its corresponding hyperbolic function, and\n\n- for any product of two trigonometric sines, change the sign of the corresponding product of hyperbolic sines.\n\n$\\displaystyle \n        \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nFor example, suppose we want to calculate the following integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\cosh^2{x} - \\sinh^2{x} \\: \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nFirst, we recall the Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n\\cos^2{x} + \\sin^2{x} = 1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the corresponding hyperbolic identity\n\n$$\n\\cosh^2{x} - \\sinh^2{x} = 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we evaluate our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {{{cosh}^{2}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x}_{⏟}}_{1}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x=x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's see another example." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186168119 :tutorial/content "$\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$We can use Osborn's rule to write down the hyperbolic equivalents of the sectant-tangent and cotangent-cosecant identities.\n\nFrom the secant-tangent identity\n\n$$\n1 + \\tan^2 x = \\sec^2 x\n$$\n\nwe have the equivalent hyperbolic identity\n\n$$\n1 - \\tanh^2 x = \\sech^2 x.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, from the cotangent-cosecant identity\n\n$$\n1+\\cot^2 x = \\csc^2 x\n$$\n\nwe have the equivalent hyperbolic identity\n\n$$\n1-\\coth^2 x  = -\\csch^2 x\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\n\\coth^2 x - 1 = \\csch^2 x.\n$$\n\nThese identities can be used to solve certain integrals involving the expressions $\\tanh^2{x},$ $\\coth^2 x,$ $\\sech^2 x,$ or $\\csch^2{x}.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167027 :activity/expected-seconds 1500.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167733 :step/math-academy-id 639523 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167630 :step/math-academy-id 639524 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167734 :step/math-academy-id 639527 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167631 :step/math-academy-id 639528 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167632 :step/math-academy-id 639531 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167633 :step/math-academy-id 639535 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192832 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cd69e9f7-e929-5fe2-b3bb-4bb36c948590" "question-dcb3950f-e511-5b2b-8452-0fa93d40b2ff"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-cd69e9f7-e929-5fe2-b3bb-4bb36c948590" :question/id #uuid "cd69e9f7-e929-5fe2-b3bb-4bb36c948590" :question/math-academy-id "q-345553" :question/problem "$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $U$ and $V$ above. Let $X$ be a $2\\times 3$ standardized observation matrix, where each row represents one observation and each column represents one feature. Given that $X=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $X,$ what is the third principal component of the data?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the unit eigenvectors of the covariance matrix $C$ are called the principal components of the data. If \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}>{\\lambda }_{2}>{\\lambda }_{3}\n$$\n\nare the eigenvalues of $C$ written in descending order, then: \n\n- the $1$st principal component is the unit eigenvector ${v}_{1}$ corresponding to the $1$st eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1},$\n\n- the $2$nd principal component is the unit eigenvector ${v}_{2}$ corresponding to the $2$nd eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2},$\n\n- the $3$rd principal component is the unit eigenvector ${v}_{3}$ corresponding to the $3$rd eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{3}.$\n\nNotice that the covariance matrix corresponding to $X$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\frac{1}{n-1}{X}^{T}X \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{n-1}(UΣ{V}^{T})^{T}(UΣ{V}^{T}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{n-1}V{Σ}^{T}({U}^{T}U)Σ{V}^{T} \\\\  & =V(\\frac{1}{n-1}{Σ}^{T}Σ){V}^{T},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere the final expression represents the diagonal form of the covariance matrix $C.$ Notice that:\n\n- $\\frac{1}{n-1}{Σ}^{T}Σ$ is a diagonal $3\\times 3$ matrix, where the entries on the main diagonal are the eigenvalues (written in descending order) of the covariance matrix $C$, and\n\n- $V$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix, whose columns are the corresponding unit eigenvectors of the covariance matrix $C.$\n\nTherefore, the columns of $V$ are the principal components of the data.\nSo, the third principal component is \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7fdc00ed-8996-53bf-b0b6-f7702bef817b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7fdc00ed-8996-53bf-b0b6-f7702bef817b" :answer-field/id #uuid "7fdc00ed-8996-53bf-b0b6-f7702bef817b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0bd13cf7-7215-5f4f-8a7c-38c0559334ff" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f890beb3-8209-55e8-a5fa-269d219fee48" "answer-8eb969dc-7431-591a-8333-b0ef3b0cc412" "answer-ae62e6b6-9922-57f6-be87-76d55ca80e65" "answer-0bd13cf7-7215-5f4f-8a7c-38c0559334ff" "answer-b1a7b6ab-39e1-5f20-9b17-720ce6944c95"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f890beb3-8209-55e8-a5fa-269d219fee48" :answer/id #uuid "f890beb3-8209-55e8-a5fa-269d219fee48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8eb969dc-7431-591a-8333-b0ef3b0cc412" :answer/id #uuid "8eb969dc-7431-591a-8333-b0ef3b0cc412" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae62e6b6-9922-57f6-be87-76d55ca80e65" :answer/id #uuid "ae62e6b6-9922-57f6-be87-76d55ca80e65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0bd13cf7-7215-5f4f-8a7c-38c0559334ff" :answer/id #uuid "0bd13cf7-7215-5f4f-8a7c-38c0559334ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1a7b6ab-39e1-5f20-9b17-720ce6944c95" :answer/id #uuid "b1a7b6ab-39e1-5f20-9b17-720ce6944c95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-dcb3950f-e511-5b2b-8452-0fa93d40b2ff" :question/id #uuid "dcb3950f-e511-5b2b-8452-0fa93d40b2ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-345562" :question/problem "$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}| &  & | \\\\ {u}_{1} & ⋯ & {u}_{n} \\\\ | &  & |\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}| &  & | \\\\ {v}_{1} & ⋯ & {v}_{m} \\\\ | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $U$ and $V$ above. Let $X$ be an $n\\times m$ standardized observation matrix, where each row represents one observation and each column represents one feature. Given that $X=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $X,$ what is the second principal component of the data?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the unit eigenvectors of the covariance matrix $C$ are called the principal components of the data. If \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}>{\\lambda }_{2}>⋯\n$$\n\nare the eigenvalues of $C$ written in descending order, then: \n\n- the $1$st principal component is the unit eigenvector ${v}_{1}$ corresponding to the $1$st eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1},$\n\n- the $2$nd principal component is the unit eigenvector ${v}_{2}$ corresponding to the $2$nd eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2},$\n\n- $⋯$\n\nand so on.\n\nNotice that the covariance matrix corresponding to $X$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\frac{1}{n-1}{X}^{T}X \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{n-1}(UΣ{V}^{T})^{T}(UΣ{V}^{T}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{n-1}V{Σ}^{T}({U}^{T}U)Σ{V}^{T} \\\\  & =V(\\frac{1}{n-1}{Σ}^{T}Σ){V}^{T},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere the final expression represents the diagonal form of the covariance matrix $C.$ Notice that:\n\n- $\\frac{1}{n-1}{Σ}^{T}Σ$ is a diagonal $m\\times m$ matrix, where the entries on the main diagonal are the eigenvalues (written in descending order) of the covariance matrix $C$, and\n\n- $V$ is a $m\\times m$ matrix, whose columns are the corresponding unit eigenvectors of the covariance matrix $C.$\n\nTherefore, the columns of $V$ are the principal components of the data.\nSo, the second principal component is ${v}_{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3a0ee814-fca1-58c8-8cc1-dbfe10fc9460"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3a0ee814-fca1-58c8-8cc1-dbfe10fc9460" :answer-field/id #uuid "3a0ee814-fca1-58c8-8cc1-dbfe10fc9460" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-feb49a45-3299-531f-989b-c646c0d9773a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c6427590-8b6b-5345-bd73-92d79f31db5a" "answer-07b599b3-e5fb-55be-8b4a-64cf19160660" "answer-feb49a45-3299-531f-989b-c646c0d9773a" "answer-c54575f9-512e-55ef-a0c7-e74be9d25000" "answer-89ae6ffb-c4b7-5567-8681-07205f0f211d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6427590-8b6b-5345-bd73-92d79f31db5a" :answer/id #uuid "c6427590-8b6b-5345-bd73-92d79f31db5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-07b599b3-e5fb-55be-8b4a-64cf19160660" :answer/id #uuid "07b599b3-e5fb-55be-8b4a-64cf19160660" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}_{2}{u}_{2}^{T}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-feb49a45-3299-531f-989b-c646c0d9773a" :answer/id #uuid "feb49a45-3299-531f-989b-c646c0d9773a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{v}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c54575f9-512e-55ef-a0c7-e74be9d25000" :answer/id #uuid "c54575f9-512e-55ef-a0c7-e74be9d25000" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{v}_{2}^{T}{v}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-89ae6ffb-c4b7-5567-8681-07205f0f211d" :answer/id #uuid "89ae6ffb-c4b7-5567-8681-07205f0f211d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{v}_{2}{v}_{2}^{T}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192833 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a62d30b2-87c9-5394-8f0b-7a8e71495548" "question-6923f3da-7346-5c88-a6fe-bd6d1873e88f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186193317 :question/problem "A scientist measured $5$ particular features, ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{5},$ for each athlete among a group of athletes. The collected data was stored in the standardized observation matrix $X,$ where each row contains measurements for a particular athlete.\nThe singular values of $X$ are \n\n$$\n{\\sigma }_{1}=5,\\,{\\sigma }_{2}=2,\\,{\\sigma }_{3}=1,\\,{\\sigma }_{4}=0.5,\\,{\\sigma }_{5}=0.1.\n$$\n\nThe scientist then converted the original observation matrix $X$ into a new matrix $Y$ using the equation $Y=X{V}_{2},$ where ${V}_{2}$ is the $5\\times 2$ matrix consisting of the first two principal components of the data. What percentage of the original variance is preserved in the new transformed matrix $Y$ compared to the initial observation matrix $X?$" :question/worked-solution "Let $V$ be the matrix of principal components. Then, applying the change of variables\n\n$$\nY=XV\n$$\n\nwe can convert our observation matrix $X$ into a new matrix $Y$ of (linearly) transformed observations such that\n\n- the covariance matrix of $Y$ is diagonal (meaning that the new features ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{5}$ are uncorrelated),\n\n- the features ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{5}$ are arranged in order of decreasing variance, and\n\n- the squares of the singular values ${\\sigma }_{1}^{2},{\\sigma }_{2}^{2},…,{\\sigma }_{5}^{2}$ represent the variances in the respective features ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{5}.$\n\nNow, the total variance over all features is proportional to the sum of the squared singular values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Total} & ∝{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sigma }_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =(5)^{2}+(2)^{2}+(1)^{2}+(0.5)^{2}+(0.1)^{2} \\\\  & =30.26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the scientist used only the first two principal components, the remaining variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Remaining} & ∝{\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{\\sigma }_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =(5)^{2}+(2)^{2} \\\\  & =29.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our required percentage can be computed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{Remaining}}{\\text{Total}} & =\\frac{29}{30.26} \\\\  & ≈0.958 \\\\  & =95.8%.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186191829 :answer-field/correct 17592186191832 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-a62d30b2-87c9-5394-8f0b-7a8e71495548" :question/id #uuid "a62d30b2-87c9-5394-8f0b-7a8e71495548" :question/math-academy-id "q-345594" :question/problem "An epidemiologist measured $4$ particular features, ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4},$ for each disease affecting a specific population. The collected data was stored in the standardized observation matrix $X,$ where each row contains measurements for a particular individual.\nThe singular values of $X$ are \n\n$$\n{\\sigma }_{1}=11,\\,{\\sigma }_{2}=7,\\,{\\sigma }_{3}=5,\\,{\\sigma }_{4}=2.\n$$\n\nThe epidemiologist then converted the original observation matrix $X$ into a new matrix $Y$ using the equation $Y=X{V}_{1},$ where ${V}_{1}$ is the $4\\times 1$ matrix consisting of the first principal component of the data. What percentage of the original variance is preserved in the new transformed matrix $Y$ compared to the initial observation matrix $X?$" :question/worked-solution "Let $V$ be the matrix of principal components. Then, applying the change of variables\n\n$$\nY=XV\n$$\n\nwe can convert our observation matrix $X$ into a new matrix $Y$ of (linearly) transformed observations such that\n\n- the covariance matrix of $Y$ is diagonal (meaning that the new features ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{4}$ are uncorrelated),\n\n- the features ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},{y}_{3},{y}_{4}$ are arranged in order of decreasing variance, and\n\n- the squares of the singular values ${\\sigma }_{1}^{2},{\\sigma }_{2}^{2},{\\sigma }_{3}^{2},{\\sigma }_{4}^{2}$ represent the variances in the respective features ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},{y}_{3},{y}_{4}.$\n\nNow, the total variance over all features is proportional to the sum of the squared singular values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Total} & ∝{\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}{\\sigma }_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =(11)^{2}+(7)^{2}+(5)^{2}+(2)^{2} \\\\  & =199\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the epidemiologist used only the first principal component, the remaining variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Remaining} & ∝{\\sum }_{i=1}^{1}{\\sigma }_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =(11)^{2} \\\\  & =121.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our required percentage can be computed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{Remaining}}{\\text{Total}} & =\\frac{121}{199} \\\\  & ≈0.608 \\\\  & =60.8%.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f239ec3f-54ad-5f78-85ed-e887372ab958"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f239ec3f-54ad-5f78-85ed-e887372ab958" :answer-field/id #uuid "f239ec3f-54ad-5f78-85ed-e887372ab958" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dccecae2-fe53-5ef0-8dd7-5f7144995552" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a003e2d0-0b5a-564f-bbea-c1c7cd17d282" "answer-49c18a90-d0ab-5db3-907e-9d6d19ce5251" "answer-dccecae2-fe53-5ef0-8dd7-5f7144995552" "answer-534fc293-1b38-5991-9c40-35df9573a0ef" "answer-f21bf8a8-668c-531d-a786-a924eb2ffa9b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a003e2d0-0b5a-564f-bbea-c1c7cd17d282" :answer/id #uuid "a003e2d0-0b5a-564f-bbea-c1c7cd17d282" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "57.1%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49c18a90-d0ab-5db3-907e-9d6d19ce5251" :answer/id #uuid "49c18a90-d0ab-5db3-907e-9d6d19ce5251" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "58.3%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dccecae2-fe53-5ef0-8dd7-5f7144995552" :answer/id #uuid "dccecae2-fe53-5ef0-8dd7-5f7144995552" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60.8%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-534fc293-1b38-5991-9c40-35df9573a0ef" :answer/id #uuid "534fc293-1b38-5991-9c40-35df9573a0ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "63.1%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f21bf8a8-668c-531d-a786-a924eb2ffa9b" :answer/id #uuid "f21bf8a8-668c-531d-a786-a924eb2ffa9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "71.2%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6923f3da-7346-5c88-a6fe-bd6d1873e88f" :question/id #uuid "6923f3da-7346-5c88-a6fe-bd6d1873e88f" :question/math-academy-id "q-345609" :question/problem "An economist measured $4$ particular features, ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4},$ for each currency in a collection under devaluation. The collected data was stored in the standardized observation matrix $X,$ where each row contains measurements for a particular currency.\nThe singular values of $X$ are \n\n$$\n{\\sigma }_{1}=12,\\,{\\sigma }_{2}=7,\\,{\\sigma }_{3}=3,\\,{\\sigma }_{4}=1.\n$$\n\nThe economist then converted the original observation matrix $X$ into a new matrix $Y$ using the equation $Y=X{V}_{1},$ where ${V}_{1}$ is the $4\\times 1$ matrix consisting of the first principal component of the data. What percentage of the original variance is preserved in the new transformed matrix $Y$ compared to the initial observation matrix $X?$" :question/worked-solution "Let $V$ be the matrix of principal components. Then, applying the change of variables\n\n$$\nY=XV\n$$\n\nwe can convert our observation matrix $X$ into a new matrix $Y$ of (linearly) transformed observations such that\n\n- the covariance matrix of $Y$ is diagonal (meaning that the new features ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{4}$ are uncorrelated),\n\n- the features ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},{y}_{3},{y}_{4}$ are arranged in order of decreasing variance, and\n\n- the squares of the singular values ${\\sigma }_{1}^{2},{\\sigma }_{2}^{2},{\\sigma }_{3}^{2},{\\sigma }_{4}^{2}$ represent the variances in the respective features ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},{y}_{3},{y}_{4}.$\n\nNow, the total variance over all features is proportional to the sum of the squared singular values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Total} & ∝{\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}{\\sigma }_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =(12)^{2}+(7)^{2}+(3)^{2}+(1)^{2} \\\\  & =203\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the economist used only the first principal component, the remaining variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Remaining} & ∝{\\sum }_{i=1}^{1}{\\sigma }_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =(12)^{2} \\\\  & =144.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our required percentage can be computed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{Remaining}}{\\text{Total}} & =\\frac{144}{203} \\\\  & ≈0.709 \\\\  & =70.9%.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-332d328e-144d-5da5-910d-9c9b357e23b6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-332d328e-144d-5da5-910d-9c9b357e23b6" :answer-field/id #uuid "332d328e-144d-5da5-910d-9c9b357e23b6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8458816f-8b48-5cde-9d4a-33d4e2eff2af" :answer-